  "_why": "PRECISION FIX ONLY — no behaviour change. v2 froze survival_mass at 3 decimals, so the conservation CEILING written as 'ratio <= 1 + 1e-9' could not resolve better than 1.7e-4 of ratio: breaking the live ratio to 1.0000001 left the guard green. A check cannot be finer than the number it reads. survival_mass and conservation_ratio are now frozen at 6 decimals and the ceiling epsilon is 1e-6, which sits above the 8e-8 rounding granularity and far below any real violation. This is rule 10b applied to the fix for rule 10b: the first ceiling claimed a precision its input did not carry. Numbers are otherwise identical to v2 to 3dp. v1 and v2 both stay on the books."
